0038: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0039:     """
0040:     Connect adjacent aligned red hollow markers by painting blue straight segments through the empty gaps between them.
0041: 
0042:     Input structure
0043:     - The background is the dominant color, and the input foreground has exactly one color.
0044:     - Each foreground object is an 8-connected four-pixel hollow plus: a 3x3 marker with only the north, south, east, and west arm pixels present.
0045:     - Some marker centers share a row or column, with background cells between the opposing outer arms of adjacent markers.
0046: 
0047:     Rule
0048:     - Compute the empty center of each marker.
0049:     - For each row, sort the marker centers left to right and paint blue over the background cells between each adjacent pair's right and left arms.
0050:     - For each column, sort the marker centers top to bottom and paint blue over the background cells between each adjacent pair's bottom and top arms.
0051: 
0052:     Key insight
0053:     - The missing centers are anchors for a visibility graph: only neighboring anchors on the same row or column are connected, so a marker between two others blocks any longer-range connection.
